      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we call process_rx_data() when the chip select is disabled, it will load up the TX FIFO with bytes that will be clocked out at the beginning of the *next* transaction. \n\nDoes the TCG SPI Protocol spec say to abort the transaction if the CS disables early, or to just pause it?",
